      "on_screen_text": "25,000 vs 2,000",
      "narration": "Yoshimoto's army is usually counted at about twenty-five thousand men. Some sources say more. Nobunaga could gather maybe two or three thousand. On paper, this wasn't a war. It was a formality.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
