          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "1. Only fight part of the army",
      "narration": "So how did two thousand beat twenty-five thousand? First, Nobunaga never had to fight all twenty-five thousand. Yoshimoto's army was spread out over miles of roads and forts. At Okehazama, Nobunaga only had to beat the part protecting the lord.",
      "word_count": 40
    },
